"# About Healthy Housing and Vector Control — Karl transcript

**Karl path:** New: About us → Content
**Decision:** no review recorded
**Page key:** \`aboutHhvcTeam\` · **Slug:** \`sf.gov/departments--healthy-housing-and-vector-control--about\` · **Type:** About us

**NOT APPROVED — do not publish from this transcript.** Approval in this tool is per page, not per field, so nothing below is signed off.

> Every keystroke below is yours to make. This file is an export, not an approval, and nothing here has been written to Karl.

### Title — \`title\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

About Healthy Housing and Vector Control

### Primary agency — \`primary_agency\` [FLAG] — page not approved

_U6 — supply the parent Agency page by hand; the mockup has no field for it._

### Information — \`about_info\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

Who we are

**Text:**

Healthy Housing and Vector Control is an Environmental Health team in San Francisco. We inspect housing conditions and respond to pest and vector reports.

Our staff include Environmental Health Inspectors and Environmental Health Technicians. They investigate complaints, conduct inspections, and work with tenants and property owners to fix Health Code Article 11 violations.

### Information — \`about_info\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

What we do

**Text:**

Our work covers:

- Investigating reports of rats, mice, insects, garbage, and other housing health conditions
- Inspecting apartments, hotels, and emergency shelters under Health Code Article 11
- Following up on Notices of Violation until conditions are corrected
- Answering questions from tenants and property owners about healthy housing requirements
- Offering free integrated pest management education for community groups and schools

### Information — \`about_info\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

How the team is organized

**Text:**

Healthy Housing and Vector Control is part of the Environmental Health branch of the San Francisco Department of Public Health.

- **Environmental Health Inspectors** investigate reports, conduct inspections, and issue Notices of Violation.
- **Environmental Health Technicians** support inspections and reinspections.
- **Program staff** answer questions, schedule education sessions, and process annual fee payments.

### Resources — \`resources\` [CHOOSE] — page not approved

