"# Get rid of cockroaches without heavy pesticides — Karl transcript

**Karl path:** New: Information → Content
**Decision:** no review recorded
**Page key:** \`cockroachesPrevention\` · **Slug:** \`sf.gov/information/get-rid-of-cockroaches-without-heavy-pesticides\` · **Type:** Information

**NOT APPROVED — do not publish from this transcript.** Approval in this tool is per page, not per field, so nothing below is signed off.

> Every keystroke below is yours to make. This file is an export, not an approval, and nothing here has been written to Karl.

### Page title — \`title\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Page title:**

Get rid of cockroaches without heavy pesticides

### Description — \`description\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Description:**

Learn why sprays do not work, how to take away what cockroaches need, and how to use baits safely.

### Primary agency — \`primary_agency\` [FLAG] — page not approved

_U6 — supply the parent Agency page by hand. Where the mockup names the agency it is text, not a page reference, and Karl requires a page: for HHVC pages that is sf.gov/departments--healthy-housing-and-vector-control._

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

Who this information is for

**Text:**

- This page is for tenants and residents dealing with cockroaches, especially in apartment buildings.

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

Why cockroaches matter

**Text:**

Cockroach droppings and shed skins get into the air and can trigger asthma, especially in children who live in apartment buildings.

The German cockroach is the most common kind in San Francisco homes. It lives indoors, near food and water, and spreads quickly.

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

Why sprays and bug bombs make it worse

**Text:**

Sprays and bug bombs only kill the cockroaches they touch. They also drive the rest deeper into walls and into your neighbors' units, and the cockroaches come back later.

Many cockroaches no longer die from the chemicals in common store-bought sprays.

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

Take away food and water

**Text:**

Cockroaches can live on tiny crumbs and drops of water. The less they find, the faster other steps will work.

- **Store food in sealed containers**, like glass jars or plastic containers that snap shut.
- **Keep flour, rice, and nuts in the fridge** if you store them for a long time.
- **Clean up crumbs, grease, and spills right away.** Do not leave dirty dishes out overnight.
- **Use a trash can with a tight lid** and a liner, and take trash out every day.
- **Fix leaks and wipe up water** around sinks, tubs, and the water heater.

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

Take away hiding places

**Text:**

- **Get rid of cardboard boxes, paper bags, and piles of paper.** Cockroaches hide and lay eggs in them.
- **Vacuum cracks and corners.** Start high and work down. A vacuum with a HEPA filter keeps allergens out of the air. Seal the vacuum bag and throw it out.
- **Clean small appliances.** Cockroaches hide in toasters, microwaves, and clocks. Unplug them, then vacuum and wipe them out.
- **Check used appliances and furniture** before you bring them home.

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

Use baits and traps instead of sprays

**Text:**

Baits work slowly, but they work. Cockroaches eat the bait and carry it back to where they hide. It can take a week or two to see full results.

- **Use bait stations or gel bait** from a hardware store. Put them under the sink, behind the fridge and stove, and inside cabinets. Put gel in pea-sized dabs about every foot along cracks.
- **Do not spray near baits.** Spray keeps cockroaches away from the bait.
- **Use sticky traps to see where they are.** Check them every few days and move baits to the busiest spots.
- **Replace bait stations every 2 to 3 months** and sticky traps every 2 weeks. Switch to a different bait brand each year.

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

Use products safely

**Text:**

- **Kill cockroaches you see with soapy water.** It works on contact without the risks of a spray.
- **Keep baits away from children and pets**, and read the label before you use any product.
- **Choose products labeled "Caution."** Avoid products labeled "Warning" or "Danger."

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

Your landlord's part

**Text:**

Cockroaches move between units through gaps around pipes, under sinks, and along walls. In an apartment building, the whole building may need treatment.

Owners must keep buildings free of pests and seal the gaps cockroaches use. Cockroaches can squeeze through cracks as small as 1/8 inch.

- **Tell your landlord in writing** where you see cockroaches.
- **You can seal small cracks yourself** with caulk, such as gaps around pipes under the sink. Do not use spray foam.
- **Ask for a licensed pest control company** that uses baits and sealing, not just sprays.
- **If nothing starts within 72 hours, report it.** [Report cockroaches or other insects](insectsReport)

**Links in this text — recreate each with the Link tool, do not paste them:**

- "Report cockroaches or other insects" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → Internal link → "Report cockroaches or other insects"

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

Learn more about cockroaches

**Text:**

The University of California Statewide Integrated Pest Management Program (UC IPM) publishes detailed, science-based guides.

- [UC IPM: Cockroaches](https://ipm.ucanr.edu/home-and-landscape/cockroaches/). How to identify the kind you have and control it.
- [UC IPM: Understanding pesticides](https://ipm.ucanr.edu/home-and-landscape/understanding-pesticides/). How to read a label and lower your risk.
- [SF Environment: How can I control insect pests in my house?](https://www.sfenvironment.org/how-can-i-control-insect-pests-my-house)
- [SF Environment: Pest management in your home (PDF)](https://www.sfenvironment.org/media/13819). A handout in English, Spanish, and Chinese.
- [UC IPM: Recursos en español](https://ipm.ucanr.edu/IPMPROJECT/recursos-espanol.html). Guías sobre plagas en español.

**Links in this text — recreate each with the Link tool, do not paste them:**

- "UC IPM: Cockroaches" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → External link
- "UC IPM: Understanding pesticides" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → External link
- "SF Environment: How can I control insect pests in my house?" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → External link
- "SF Environment: Pest management in your home (PDF)" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → External link
- "UC IPM: Recursos en español" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → External link

### Topics — \`topics\` [TYPE] — page not approved

_topicTag is unmapped metadata — the stored values are Agency labels, not Topic chooser references. Do not paste one into this chooser._

### Related — \`related\` [CHOOSE] — page not approved

