### Cost — \`cost\` [TYPE] — page not approved

_Choose the Cost radio first (Free, Flat fee, Range, Minimum and up, None) — all five variants end at this same description field._

**Cost description:**

Free

### Things to Know — \`things_to_know\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Block 1 — Title:**

What we check

**Block 1 — Text:**

We look for water sources on private property, if the owner or resident lets us in, and in public spaces. We also check public catch basins near your report for mosquito larvae.

**Block 2 — Title:**

An inspector may ask to come in

**Block 2 — Text:**

To find the water source, an inspector may need to enter a yard or property. Include a phone number or email so we can arrange access.

### What to Do — \`what_to_do\` [TYPE] — page not approved

_The mockup heading "What to do" is not typed anywhere — Karl's What to Do panel carries its own label. Each step below becomes one Section block._

_A step with text, a button and a callout becomes ONE Section block whose Section specifics holds a Text, a Button link and a Callout as siblings — not fields on the step._

**Section 1 — Section title:**

Start your report

**Section 1 — Section specifics → Text:**

Use 311 to report mosquitoes or standing water to the City. If the problem is urgent, report now. You can report mosquitoes where you live or standing water you see nearby, or report for someone else.

Live in an SRO or residential hotel? Report the same way. One clerk takes every report and assigns SRO cases to senior inspectors.

**Section 1 — Section specifics → Button link → Link text:**

Report through 311

**Section 1 — Button link → destination:**

None

**Section 2 — Section title:**

Tell us where the water is

**Section 2 — Section specifics → Text:**

Only share the details that apply to your situation:

- **What you saw:** Biting mosquitoes, or small wriggling larvae in water.
- **Where the water is:** Buckets, planters, saucers, clogged gutters, fountains, pools, or a street catch basin.
- **The address:** Where the water is, and whether it is on private property or in a public space.
- **Access:** Who can let an inspector into the yard or property, if you know.
- **Your contact info:** Leave a phone number or email if you want an inspector to contact you.

**Callout (rich text, no title field):**

We never share your name or contact information. You do not need to send photos.

**Section 3 — Section title:**

See a dead bird? Report it to the State

**Section 3 — Section specifics → Text:**

Dead birds help track West Nile virus. The State West Nile virus program collects these reports, not 311.

**Section 3 — Section specifics → Button link → Link text:**

Report a dead bird

**Section 3 — Button link → destination:**

External URL → https://westnile.ca.gov/report

### Accordion title and text — \`supporting_information\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

While you wait: tips to help with the problem

**Text:**

It may take us a few weekdays to get back to you. In the meantime, here are a few things you can do to help with the problem.

- **Dump standing water:** Empty buckets, planters, saucers, and toys at least once a week.
- **Clear gutters:** Clogged gutters hold water where mosquitoes breed.
- **Fix screens:** Repair holes in window and door screens.

