"# Pay your annual Healthy Housing fee for apartment buildings — Karl transcript

**Karl path:** New: Transaction → Content
**Decision:** no review recorded
**Page key:** \`payFee\` · **Slug:** \`sf.gov/pay-your-annual-healthy-housing-fee-apartment-buildings\` · **Type:** Transaction

**NOT APPROVED — do not publish from this transcript.** Approval in this tool is per page, not per field, so nothing below is signed off.

> Every keystroke below is yours to make. This file is an export, not an approval, and nothing here has been written to Karl.

### Page title — \`title\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Page title:**

Pay your annual Healthy Housing fee for apartment buildings

### Description — \`description\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Description:**

Pay your annual Healthy Housing fee if you own an apartment building with 3 or more rental units.

### Primary agency — \`primary_agency\` [CHOOSE] — page not approved

_U6, narrowed — the mockup names the agency as text, not as a page reference, and Karl requires a page. Choose the parent Agency page: HHVC was approved for its own Agency page (sf.gov/departments--healthy-housing-and-vector-control), so that is the value for HHVC pages rather than Environmental Health or DPH. Those two remain Partner agencies._

1. Choose page: "Healthy Housing and Vector Control"

### Cost — \`cost\` [FLAG] — page not approved

_Cost description is 128 characters; Karl caps this field at 120. Shorten it before typing._

_Choose the Cost radio first (Free, Flat fee, Range, Minimum and up, None) — all five variants end at this same description field._

**Cost description:**

Annual fee based on rental unit count — $103 (3 units) up to $808 (more than 30 units). Check your invoice for the exact amount.

### Things to Know — \`things_to_know\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Block 1 — Title:**

Who must pay

**Block 1 — Text:**

You must pay if you own an apartment building with 3 or more rental units. This applies even if you live there.

**Block 2 — Title:**

Annual fee vs. reinspection fees

**Block 2 — Text:**

The annual fee is separate from reinspection fees, which only apply if an inspection finds an uncorrected violation.

### What to Do — \`what_to_do\` [TYPE] — page not approved

_The mockup heading "What to do" is not typed anywhere — Karl's What to Do panel carries its own label. Each step below becomes one Section block._

_A step with text, a button and a callout becomes ONE Section block whose Section specifics holds a Text, a Button link and a Callout as siblings — not fields on the step._

**Section 1 — Section title:**

Check your invoice and whether the fee applies

**Section 1 — Section specifics → Text:**

Environmental Health mails an invoice each year. Check the property address, the number of rental units, the amount due, and the due date.

You need to pay if you own an apartment building with 3 or more rental units during the billing year.

- If you own and live in the building, count the rental units. If you rent 3 or more units, you still need to pay.
- If you rent fewer than 3 units, complete, sign, and return the certification on your invoice.
- Vacant units and units occupied by relatives still count as rental units.
- Condominium, commercial, and tenancy-in-common buildings do not pay this fee. Send the proof requested on your invoice.
- [Property owner responsibilities](ownerHub)

**Section 2 — Section title:**

Confirm your annual fee

**Section 2 — Section specifics → Text:**

Your annual fee is based on the number of rental units. Check your invoice for the exact amount and due date.

- 3 units: $103
- 4-6 units: $129
- 7-10 units: $175
- 11-15 units: $350
- 16-20 units: $485
- 21-30 units: $688
- More than 30 units: $808

**Callout (rich text, no title field):**

**Annual fee and reinspection fees are different:** the annual fee supports Healthy Housing inspections. If an inspection finds an uncorrected violation, a separate reinspection fee may apply. It is $256 per hour for an Environmental Health Inspector, or $234 per hour for a Technician. Additional half-hours cost $128 and $115.

**Section 3 — Section title:**

Pay online, in person, or by mail

**Section 3 — Section specifics → Text:**

Pay online with your invoice information, or use the payment instructions on your invoice.

- **In person:** pay by check, cash, or money order at City Hall, Room 140, 1 Dr. Carlton B. Goodlett Place.
- **By mail:** make a check or money order payable to "Department of Public Health." Write your invoice number on it and mail it to P.O. Box 7429, San Francisco, CA 94120.

**Section 3 — Section specifics → Button link → Link text:**

Pay your fee online

**Section 3 — Button link → destination:**

External URL → https://services.paysf.co/service/healthy-housing-fee

**Section 4 — Section title:**

Correct an invoice or update your information

**Section 4 — Section specifics → Text:**

Check the property address, mailing address, owner, building type, and number of rental units on your invoice. Contact Environmental Health before you pay if anything is wrong.

- For a unit-count correction, tell us the correct number of rental units and pay the fee for that number.
- If the count is wrong because you live in a unit, include a copy of your most recent PG&E bill.
- For an ownership change, provide the escrow date and the new owner’s name and mailing address.
- For a mailing-address change, include the property address and block and lot number, or the invoice number.
- Email healthyhousing@sf.gov or call 415-252-3800. Also report ownership changes to the Assessor-Recorder’s Office.

**Section 5 — Section title:**

Pay by the due date or contact us

**Section 5 — Section specifics → Text:**

Pay within 30 days of the invoice due date. Keep your invoice number or property address if you need help with your account.

- A $10 late penalty applies after 30 days.
- A $30 late penalty applies after 60 days.
- Unpaid balances may accrue 1.5% interest per month and may become a property lien.

**Callout (rich text, no title field):**

**What the annual fee supports:** Healthy Housing uses these fees to support inspections of apartment buildings. Inspectors look at common areas, yards, garbage storage areas, and lobbies. They check for conditions that may support pests or create housing health hazards.

**Links in this text — recreate each with the Link tool, do not paste them:**

- "Property owner responsibilities" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → Internal link → "Property owner responsibilities"

### Related — \`related\` [CHOOSE] — page not approved

_This block publishes the destination page’s title and a link, and NOTHING else. Choose the page and type no description._

1. Choose page: "Healthy housing conditions" (\`healthyHousingTopic\` → /sf.gov/topics--healthy-housing-conditions)

### Partner agencies — \`partner_agencies\` [CHOOSE] — page not approved

_A page chooser restricted to Agency pages. These entries name real sf.gov department pages outside this mockup, so search Karl for each by title._

1. Choose page: "Environmental Health"

### Topics — \`topics\` [TYPE] — page not approved

_topicTag is unmapped metadata — the stored values are Agency labels, not Topic chooser references._

### Redirect this page to — \`redirect_url\` [TYPE] — page not approved

_Disabled by design — a ConditionalReadOnlyFieldPanel. Never type into it._

### Promote → For search engines — \`promote\` [TYPE] — page not approved

