"# Rat-free blocks — Karl transcript

**Karl path:** New: Campaign → Content
**Decision:** no review recorded
**Page key:** \`ratFreeBlocks\` · **Slug:** \`sf.gov/rat-free-blocks\` · **Type:** Campaign

**NOT APPROVED — do not publish from this transcript.** Approval in this tool is per page, not per field, so nothing below is signed off.

> Every keystroke below is yours to make. This file is an export, not an approval, and nothing here has been written to Karl.

### Title — \`title\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

Rat-free blocks

### Primary agency — \`primary_agency\` [FLAG] — page not approved

_U6 — supply the parent Agency page by hand; the mockup has no field for it._

### Spotlight 1 — \`spotlight_1\` [TYPE] — page not approved

_Image alignment (Side by side / Full width) and Image position (Right / Left) are both required radios with no mockup equivalent — choose them by hand._

_Campaign shows up to 2 Spotlights. That is a rendering and editorial cap, not one the form enforces._

**Spotlight title:**

Take away what rats live on

**Spotlight description:**

Rats do not respond to one clean yard. They respond to a block that removes food, water, and shelter at the same time.

**Button link — Link text:**

Report rats and mice

**Button link — destination:**

SF.gov page → "Report rats or mice"

### Spotlight 2 — \`spotlight_2\` [TYPE] — page not approved

_Spotlight 1 and Spotlight 2 are two independent top-level fields, not one repeatable field with two slots, so a third spotlight concept has nowhere to go._

_Link text is 26 characters, over the 25-character limit. Shorten it. The field itself accepts 255, so an over-length label saves without error — the form does not enforce this and will not catch it for you._

_Image alignment (Side by side / Full width) and Image position (Right / Left) are both required radios with no mockup equivalent — choose them by hand._

_Campaign shows up to 2 Spotlights. That is a rendering and editorial cap, not one the form enforces._

**Spotlight title:**

For owners and managers

**Spotlight description:**

Under Article 11, rodent conditions on a property you own or manage are yours to correct. This applies whether or not anyone has reported them.

**Button link — Link text:**

See owner responsibilities

**Button link — destination:**

SF.gov page → "Property owner responsibilities"

### Top facts — \`facts_title + fact_items\` [TYPE] — page not approved

_Fact items carry no reviewer overlay — this tool records no edit for them, so these are the authored values rather than reviewed ones._

**Facts title:**

What a block can do together

**Fact 1 — title:**

Food

**Fact 1 — text:**

Close bins fully. Keep pet food and bird seed indoors. Pick fruit up off the ground.

**Fact 2 — title:**

Water

**Fact 2 — text:**

Fix outdoor leaks and drips. Empty anything holding standing water after rain.

**Fact 3 — title:**

Harborage

**Fact 3 — text:**

Clear dense ground cover, woodpiles, and clutter along fences and foundations.

**Fact 4 — title:**

Entry

**Fact 4 — text:**

Seal gaps around pipes, vents, and doors. A rat fits through a gap the size of a quarter.

### Additional content — \`additional_content\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

Start with your own block

**Text:**

A coordinated week does more than a year of single properties acting alone. Neighbors, and neighborhood or merchant associations, do not need permission from the City to organize one.

- Agree a week when everyone clears clutter and checks their bins.
- Walk the block together afterwards and look for the gaps that remain.
- Report what is left, especially anything on a property no one is maintaining: [rats or mice](rodentsReport), [animal waste](animalWasteReport), or [garbage, clutter, or overgrown plants](garbageReport).
- Pick up pet waste daily. It feeds rats.

**Links in this text — recreate each with the Link tool, do not paste them:**

