"# Correct a violation and close your case — Karl transcript

**Karl path:** New: Step by step → Content
**Decision:** no review recorded
**Page key:** \`stepCorrectViolation\` · **Slug:** \`sf.gov/step-by-step/correct-a-violation-and-close-your-case\` · **Type:** Step by step

**NOT APPROVED — do not publish from this transcript.** Approval in this tool is per page, not per field, so nothing below is signed off.

> Every keystroke below is yours to make. This file is an export, not an approval, and nothing here has been written to Karl.

### Title — \`title\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

Correct a violation and close your case

### Primary agency — \`primary_agency\` [FLAG] — page not approved

_U6 — the mockup has no primary_agency field, and Karl requires it. Supply the parent Agency page by hand: HHVC was approved for its own Agency page (sf.gov/departments--healthy-housing-and-vector-control), so that is the value for HHVC pages rather than Environmental Health or DPH. Those two remain Partner agencies._

### Description — \`description\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Description:**

The steps from a Notice of Violation to a passed re-inspection, and who is responsible at each one.

### Intro — \`intro\` [TYPE] — page not approved

⚠ Inferred mapping — verify the destination before saving.

_Step by step has no things_to_know and no page-level cost, so a Transaction page's whatToKnow has nowhere to go here. Intro is the one free-text slot before the steps, which makes it where an audience line ("Who this information is for") belongs on this type._

_Inferred mapping — the field map documents this panel only for supporting/flat sections. Transaction has no generic body stream and this is its only repeatable Title-and-text panel, so verify the destination before saving._

**Title:**

Who this information is for

**Text:**

This page is the whole arc of one case, from the notice arriving to the case closing. Each step says who is responsible for it.

- Property owners and managers named on a notice
- Tenants with actions listed on a notice
- Anyone coordinating the work on a building

### Steps — \`steps\` [TYPE] — page not approved

_The block 27 mockup karl notes were describing. Unlike Transaction's what_to_do Section, a Step carries its own cost and time, and a Transaction link chooser — which is how a Step by step points at the Transaction pages holding the detail._

_The mockup heading "What to do" is not typed anywhere — Karl's What to Do panel carries its own label. Each step below becomes one Section block._

_Each step is one Step block: its Title, then its Step description (text and bullets together). A step can link to one Transaction page or none, chosen with the page chooser rather than typed._

**Step 1 — Title:**

Read the notice and find your deadline

**Step 1 — Step description:**

The notice lists the conditions to correct and the date they are due. That date governs everything below — this page does not set one.

- Check which actions are assigned to the owner, to the manager, and to a tenant.
- A notice can list actions for the building, shared areas, or a specific unit.
- [Health Code Article 11 in plain language](article11Guide)

**Step 2 — Title:**

Owners and managers: arrange the work

**Step 2 — Step description:**

Work in shared areas, structural repairs, professional pest treatment, and garbage removal are the owner or manager’s to arrange.

- Use a licensed pest control operator when professional treatment is required.
- Do not wait on a tenant’s task before starting work you control.
- [Property owner responsibilities](ownerHub)
- [Integrated pest management for property owners and managers](ownerGuidance)
- [Article 11 compliance for property owners](article11Compliance)

**Step 3 — Title:**

Tenants: prepare the unit and allow access

**Step 3 — Step description:**

Unit preparation and access are the tenant’s part. Treatment that cannot reach the unit does not close the violation.

- Follow the preparation instructions you were given before a treatment visit.
- Allow properly noticed access for inspection or work.
- A Notice of Violation does not change a tenant’s right to safe and habitable housing.
- [Prepare your unit for pest treatment](stepPrepUnit)
- [What tenants need to do after a Notice of Violation](tenantNoticeSteps)
- [Tenant rights when reporting housing conditions](tenantRights)

**Step 4 — Title:**

Ask for more time before the deadline, not after

**Step 4 — Step description:**

If the work cannot be finished in time, contact the investigator named on the notice before the date passes.

They can explain the cited conditions, the deadline, and what proof of correction is needed.

- Ask early. A request made after the deadline is a different conversation.
- This page does not promise an extension — whether one is granted is the investigator’s call.

**Step 5 — Title:**

Keep proof of the work

**Step 5 — Step description:**

Photos, receipts, and pest treatment reports are what show the conditions were corrected.

- Keep records for every cited condition, not just the largest one.
- Confirm every condition listed on the notice has been addressed, not only the ones that were easiest to fix.

**Step 6 — Title:**

Pass the re-inspection

**Step 6 — Step description:**

A follow-up inspection checks whether the cited conditions were corrected. The case closes when they have been.

- An inspector reviews the specific conditions listed on your Notice of Violation to confirm whether they were corrected.
- One party finishing does not close the case while other cited conditions remain.

**Step 7 — Title:**

If it is not corrected

**Step 7 — Step description:**

Further enforcement can follow an uncorrected notice. This can include a reinspection fee where one applies, a citation, or a Director’s Hearing.

Follow the instructions and deadlines in any later notice you receive.

- [Question a Notice of Violation](appealNotice)
- [Pay a Healthy Housing citation](payCitation)
- [What happens after you report a housing or pest problem](afterReport)

**Links in this text — recreate each with the Link tool, do not paste them:**

